==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Removing F_CareTeamGating allows Alloy to construct a world where an AccessAttempt has outcome=Permitted even though no ActiveMembership links the caller to the target patient, directly violating the care-team-only authorisation rule in FR-006.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_006_CareTeamGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_006_CareTeamGating: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries allows two distinct AuditEntries to record the same AccessAttempt, modelling an overwrite or duplicate-write of an existing audit record. The AppendOnly and FR_010_AuditImmutability assertions then find a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_010_AuditImmutability, FR_012_AuditRetention
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_010_AuditImmutability: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_012_AuditRetention: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditCompleteness allows an AccessAttempt to exist with no corresponding AuditEntry, directly violating the always-on audit obligation in FR-008 and the audit-before-access rule in FR-013.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit, FR_013_AuditBeforeAccess
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AuditBeforeAccess: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ByteEquivalentNotFound  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_ByteEquivalentNotFound.als
    rationale: Removing F_ByteEquivalentNotFound allows a Denied AccessAttempt to be assigned SuccessResponse, making the denied-access path distinguishable from the not-found path and leaking the existence of the patient to an unauthorised clinician.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_007_ByteEquivalentNotFound
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ByteEquivalentNotFound: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AttributionCorrectness  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AttributionCorrectness.als
    rationale: Removing F_AttributionCorrectness allows an AuditEntry's role_snapshot to differ from the actual role of the access's caller, breaking the snapshot-fidelity requirement in FR-009 (a renamed or wrong-role clinician appears in the audit log).
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_009_AuditEntryShape
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_AuditEntryShape: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilegeClinicalEndpoint  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_LeastPrivilegeClinicalEndpoint.als
    rationale: Removing F_LeastPrivilegeClinicalEndpoint allows an AuditOfficer to appear as the caller of an AccessAttempt on PostRecordsLookup, violating the role-segregation requirement that audit officers may not use the clinical endpoint.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_001_AuthRequired, FR_011_AuditVisibleToIGOnly
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_AuditVisibleToIGOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

